// The argument registers each Linux system call reads, by architecture
// and number: the count of the kernel handler's parameters, where on
// ARM a 64-bit one takes an even-aligned register pair.  Generated by
// scripts/generate_linux_syscall_arguments.py from Linux 6.1's
// system call tables and handler prototypes (original exact revision unknown).
// Incrementally updated on 2026-10-19: numbers 451-471 and bpf arities from
// Linux 7.2, commit 8d3ae59288f1e7d58d76558a6ee96d533bc5019f.
// Corrected legacy AArch64 omissions and excluded compat-only time64 numbers.
// See LinuxSyscallArguments.sources.json for the exact scope and source blobs.
// This is not a full Linux 7.2 regeneration. Unlisted numbers retain every
// argument register. Review the provenance before regenerating this file.

#ifndef NEVERD_LINUX_SYSCALL_ARGUMENTS
#define NEVERD_LINUX_SYSCALL_ARGUMENTS(Arch, Number, Count)
#endif

